Without a `verify()` call (at the end of the test or in an `afterEach`), the test will not catch an *extra, unexpected* request. A common regression in an HTTP service method is a duplicated call (`httpClient.get` invoked twice, or a retry/subscription bug firing an extra request). Your `expectOne(url).flush(mockResponse)` only asserts about *one* matching request — it does not by itself fail the test if a second request is also in flight. `verify()` is what closes that gap.

