The problem: `addItem` mutates the array in place with `this.items.push(item)`. Under `OnPush`, the component only re-checks when Angular sees a reference change on an input, a signal read in the template changes, an event handler bound in the template fires, or a mark-for-check is triggered. Pushing onto the existing array does not create a new reference, so the `@for` loop reading `items` has nothing new to detect — Angular's diffing sees the same array reference it already rendered. The added row either won't appear until some unrelated re-check happens to fire, or appears inconsistently depending on timing.

The fix is to replace the reference rather than mutate it:

```ts
