```

If neither is done, the caller would have to manually call `ChangeDetectorRef.markForCheck()` after `addItem`, which is fragile and easy to omit. The reference replacement (or signal update) is the correct fix and aligns with the OnPush contract that inputs/state are treated as immutable.

With `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`, this component will only re-render when one of its tracked inputs changes by reference, when an event handler it owns fires, or when a signal/`markForCheck()` explicitly tells Angular to re-check it. Angular's default change-detection comparison is by reference (`===`), not deep equality.

`addItem` mutates the existing array in place:

