```

The array reference `this.items` is unchanged — it's still the same array object that was there before `push` was called. Under `OnPush`, Angular compares the `items` binding against the "last known" value; since the reference is identical, it concludes nothing has changed and skips re-checking the template. The result is that the newly pushed item does not appear in the rendered `@for` loop, even though `items.length` has grown when inspected in a console. If `addItem` is triggered as a click handler on this same component, the click itself will happen to mark the component dirty, which masks the bug in that one case; but the moment `addItem` is invoked from outside the component — a service call, a parent's event, an `input()`, an interval — the update silently won't render.

